            "pair_body": "Its balanced smoke and bright acidity make Espadín the most versatile pour in the range — equally at home stirred down or chilled over a single rock.",
            "highlight_1": "Single-village production in the highlands of Oaxaca",
            "highlight_2": "Earthen-pit roasted, tahona-crushed, copper distilled",
            "highlight_3": "Small-batch — never more than 600 bottles per run",
            "highlight_4": "The ideal introduction to artesanal mezcal",
            "review_rating": "5.00",
            "review_count": "20",
            "review_quote": "\"Probably the most complex mezcal I've ever tasted. Truly special.\"",
            "review_author": "— Verified Buyer"
